id: pm-t6jl1f
title: "GH-1280: preserve literal completion across Bash versions and package helper paths"
description: "Replace Bash word re-expansion with literal prefix selection for static, dynamic, fallback and cached choices. Preserve Unicode on Bash 3.2 and byte locales, shell-quote accepted candidates to prevent command execution and globbing, refuse ambiguous quoted prefixes, and route canonical guide-shell helper paths to their plain-word transport."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-20T12:59:34.645Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-20T14:48:32.431Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-20T14:48:31.908Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-20T14:48:31.908Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: All Bash completion routes preserve literal argument values after acceptance; candidate metadata cannot execute or expand filesystem globs; ambiguous quoted prefixes produce no suggestions; native Bash 3.2 and current Bash cover byte and UTF-8 locales; required coverage and security gates pass.
parent: pm-mpbb
severity: high
environment: macOS system Bash 3.2; also literal glob corruption on current Bash
repro_steps: Generate Bash completion with a dynamic Unicode type; invoke _pm_completion for --type under Bash 3.2. Add a literal wildcard candidate in a directory with files to observe unquoted array pathname expansion.
resolution: "Delivered Bash 3.2 literal matching, safe accepted-word quoting and canonical package helper transport."
expected_result: Unicode and metacharacters remain literal through completion and command acceptance on Bash 3.2 and current Bash.
actual_result: 91 native Bash boundary cases pass; real Tab-and-Enter acceptance is literal on Bash 3.2 and 5.3; installed helpers preserve words and explicit JSON; temporary lifecycle and packed npm/npx/bunx acceptance pass.
affected_version: 2026.9.20
component: sdk-completion
